  "geometryBasis": "The named Ottawa footprint and separately mapped roof and wall subparts fix the wedge plan and its orientations. Native 1 m NRCan bare-earth and first-return elevations control the ground and the main roof planes. The museum’s corporate report establishes the 24.5 m peak.",
  "sectionBasis": "The museum’s architecture and engineering records identify exposed concrete, sod roofs, glowing copper, tilted glass and the tall Regeneration Hall. The original public-domain construction photograph establishes the permanent faceted volumes and the positions of the glazing and Morse-code apertures.",
  "limitations": [
    "The 24.5 m peak is documented. Roof slopes use measured first-return samples, with localized interpretation at steps, narrow windows and parapets below the lidar resolution.",
    "Curtain-wall subdivisions, concrete seams, copper panel widths and Morse aperture positions are approximated. The bilingual words encoded on the north fin are documented.",
    "The exterior represents the standing museum with finished grass roofs and public terrace. The archive photo was taken during construction. Site hoardings, unfinished roof surfaces and current exhibition objects are outside the modeled scope."
